{"name":"Bubble Bath","hex":"#e8e0e9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bubble bath","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bath in which an additive, usually soap, is poured directly into the water that creates bubbles; a foam bath.","The product poured in the bath to create those bubbles."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bubble_bath"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bubble bath","blocks":[{"text":"A bubble bath is a filled bathtub with a layer of soap bubbles on the surface of the water. Less commonly, aerated or carbonated baths are called bubble baths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/39/Bundesarchiv_Bild_102-09247%2C_Berlinerin_im_Schaumbad.jpg/330px-Bundesarchiv_Bild_102-09247%2C_Berlinerin_im_Schaumbad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bubble_bath"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Ringling_Circus_clown_Emmett_Kelly_in_a_bubble_bath_Sarasota%2C_Florida.jpg/500px-Ringling_Circus_clown_Emmett_Kelly_in_a_bubble_bath_Sarasota%2C_Florida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Ringling_Circus_clown_Emmett_Kelly_in_a_bubble_bath_Sarasota%2C_Florida.jpg/500px-Ringling_Circus_clown_Emmett_Kelly_in_a_bubble_bath_Sarasota%2C_Florida.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Circus clown Emmett Kelly in a bubble bath, photographed by Joseph Janney Steinmetz (c. 1955)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARingling_Circus_clown_Emmett_Kelly_in_a_bubble_bath_Sarasota%2C_Florida.jpg"}],"sounds":{"bubble bath":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9c/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Flame%2C_not_lame-bubble_bath.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"